Build mali_kbase r52p0 on Linux 7.3

- Kbuild: since 6.13 an external module builds from its own directory
  with $(src) relative to it, so do not prefix $(srctree).
- EXTRA_CFLAGS is gone from Kbuild; pass the CONFIG_MALI_* defines
  through KCFLAGS as well.
- hrtimer_init() and hrtimer_init_on_stack() are gone: hrtimer_setup().
- del_timer()/del_timer_sync() are now timer_delete()/timer_delete_sync().
- dma_fence_signal() returns void and dma_fence_ops lost fence_value_str.
- mm_get_unmapped_area() lost its mm argument.
- Only in-tree page types can be movable_ops pages, so __SetPageMovable()
  is gone: keep kbase page migration off on these kernels.

diff --git a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
index 489ea73..e736932 100644
--- a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
+++ b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 
 # make $(src) as absolute path if it is not already, by prefixing $(srctree)
 # This is to prevent any build issue due to wrong path.
-src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(srctree)/$(src),$(src))
+src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(if $(KBUILD_EXTMOD),$(abspath $(src)),$(srctree)/$(src)),$(src))
 
